Ideas taken, text not taken
---------------------------

Two ideas in this repository came from other projects: the devil's advocate
reviewer, and the seeded-defect calibration. None of their text appears here.
Both prompts and the calibration implementation were written from scratch for
this roster and this schema.

Licences were checked against each repository on 2026-09-07, not against local
copies. Of the four below, one is CC BY-NC, which would have forced this
repository to be non-commercial; two state no licence at all, so copying would
not have been permissible; and one grants use informally without carrying a
licence file. Nothing was copied from any of them regardless.

  Imbad0202/academic-research-skills — https://github.com/Imbad0202/academic-research-skills
  CC BY-NC 4.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Cheng-I Wu
  Two ideas, both used without any of its text. First, the devil's advocate:
  a panel member whose remit is to argue against the paper rather than to look
  for a class of defect. Second, its calibration mode: the principle that a
  reviewer's own error profile should be measured rather than assumed. The
  metric here is different, because that project scores accept/reject
  decisions against gold labels and robusto has no decision to score, so
  robusto measures recall on defects it plants itself. The principle is theirs.

  scunning1975/MixtapeTools — https://github.com/scunning1975/MixtapeTools
  No licence file; the repository states "Use freely. Attribution appreciated
  but not required." Its Referee 2 skill is the source of the stance that a
  review is an audit filing a report against a checklist, rather than a
  reaction. Upstream already worked this way; the resemblance is noted because
  the idea was consulted. Referee 2 was also consulted when documenting how
  robusto differs from a code-and-replication audit, since it audits the
  pipeline behind a paper rather than the manuscript.

  nikhilklath/skills
  A private repository, so the link is omitted: it would 404 for any reader
  without access. No licence stated. Its review-paper skill frames a
  pre-submission review as prioritised findings across contribution,
  identification, consistency, math, exhibits and prose. That framing informed
  how the devil's advocate is asked to rank what it finds.

  lcrawfurd/claude-skills — https://github.com/lcrawfurd/claude-skills
  No licence stated. Consulted for the same persona in a shorter form.


What this repository is not
---------------------------

It is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or reviewed by any of the projects
above. Defects in robusto are robusto's, not theirs. In particular, the
schema-contract layer that replaces provider-enforced structured output is new
here and is the most likely place for this port to behave differently from
upstream.
